---
title: Millionaire's shortbread
servings: 32
yield: 32 bars
tags: [vegetarian, make-ahead]
time: 2 hours 30 minutes
source: Chocolate Caramel Shortbread Bars by Molly Marzalek-Kelly, King Arthur Baking, https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/chocolate-caramel-shortbread-bars-recipe
---

Heat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Grease a #9x13-inch pan{} and line it with a
parchment sling.

== Shortbread ==

Beat the @unsalted butter{226%g}(cold), @light brown sugar{142%g}(packed),
@vanilla extract{1%tsp} and @table salt{1/2%tsp} ~{3%minutes} to 5 minutes,
until smooth.

Scrape the bowl, add the @all-purpose flour{240%g} and beat until shaggy and
crumbly.

Tip it into the pan, shake it level and press it firmly into an even layer.
Chill ~{15%minutes} in the freezer or 30 minutes in the fridge.

Bake ~{20%minutes} to 25 minutes, until golden brown. Let it cool.

== Caramel ==

In a #large pot{}, combine the @sweetened condensed milk{397%g},
@light brown sugar{160%g}(packed), @unsalted butter{85%g} and
@table salt{1/4%tsp}. Cook over low heat until the butter melts and it is
smooth.

Raise to medium and stir constantly until it boils. Keep stirring until it
thickens, darkens and pulls away from the sides, 225 to 240°F (107 to 115°C) on
a #thermometer{}.

Off the heat, stir in @vanilla extract{2%tsp} and spread it straight away over
the shortbread to the edges. Cool completely, about ~{1%hour} at room
temperature or 25 minutes in the fridge.

== Chocolate ==

Put the @bittersweet chocolate{170%g}(or semisweet, wafers or chips) in a
heatproof bowl. Bring the @heavy cream{170%g} to a boil and pour it over.

Leave ~{2%minutes}, add @vanilla extract{1/2%tsp} and whisk until smooth.

Spread it over the caramel to the edges. Let it set ~{20%minutes} to 30
minutes, then cut into 32 bars, 8 by 4, with a warm knife.

> Keeps a week in the fridge, airtight. Serve at room temperature.
